 .TP
 .B \-w, \-\-system
 Report systemwide memory usage summary.
+When
+.B \-\-realmem
+is not given, smem tries to read the installed DIMM size with
+.B dmidecode
+and falls back to
+.I MemTotal
+if that is not available.
+
+.TP
+.B \-W, \-\-sysdetail
+Report a more detailed systemwide breakdown (kernel modules, caches,
+tmpfs, ramfs, and a per-process shared-memory adjustment). Add the
+.B details
+column (or
+.BR \-c " all")
+for the extra metric column.
+
+.TP
+.B \-g, \-\-groupcmd
+Group processes by executable and print one row per command.
+
+.TP
+.B \-b, \-\-basename
+Show the executable name instead of the full command line. Mapping
+names are reduced to their base name as well.
+
+.TP
+.B \-q, \-\-quiet
+Suppress warnings, including missing-kernel-feature warnings and the
+notice printed when smem is not run as root.
+
+.TP
+.B \-T, \-\-totalsonly
+Show only the totals line. Implies
+.BR \-t .
 
 .SS FILTER BY
 If none of these options are included, memory usage is reported for all
@@ -93,6 +128,18 @@
 .BI "\-U " USERFILTER ", \-\-userfilter=" USERFILTER
 User filter regular expression.
 
+.TP
+.B \-i, \-\-ignorecase
+Match process, user, and mapping filters without regard to case.
+Process filters match the pid, the comm name, and the command line.
+The running smem process is omitted from a live
+.B \-P
+report so the filter does not match smem itself.
+
+.TP
+.BI "\-\-pid=" PID
+Report only this process id.
+
 .SS OUTPUT FORMATTING
 
 .TP
